{title: Immortal, Invisible, God Only Wise}
{artist: Walter Chalmers Smith / Welsh melody (St. Denio)}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: D}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}
{score: immortal-invisible-god-only-wise.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Immortal, in[G]visible, [D]God only [A]wise
In [D]light inac[G]cessible [D]hid from our [A]eyes
Most [Bm]blessed, most [A]glorious, the [D]Ancient of [G]Days
Al[D]mighty, vic[A]torious, Thy [D]great name we [A]praise [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Unresting, un[G]hasting, and [D]silent as [A]light
Nor [D]wanting, nor [G]wasting, Thou [D]rulest in [A]might
Thy [Bm]justice like [A]mountains high [D]soaring a[G]bove
Thy [D]clouds which are [A]fountains of [D]goodness and [A]love [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
To [D]all, life Thou [G]givest, to [D]both great and [A]small
In [D]all life Thou [G]livest, the [D]true life of [A]all
We [Bm]blossom and [A]flourish as [D]leaves on the [G]tree
And [D]wither and [A]perish, but [D]naught changeth [A]Thee [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Great [D]Father of [G]Glory, pure [D]Father of [A]Light
Thine [D]angels a[G]dore Thee, all [D]veiling their [A]sight
All [Bm]laud we would [A]render: O [D]help us to [G]see
'Tis [D]only the [A]splendor of [D]light hideth [A]Thee [D]
{end_of_verse}
